From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com> (ncz-os/meta-cix)
Subject: [PATCH] regulator: cix: handle unsupported pmic constraints quietly
Source: ncz-os/meta-cix
        linux-cix-sky1-ncz-7.2/patches-7.2/0181-regulator-cix-handle-unsupported-pmic-constraints-quietly.patch
Adopted: grimtickle-overlay 7.2.9; see NOTICE.md.

fwnode_get_regulator_prot_limits() left `found` uninitialised and only ever
assigned it true, never resetting it to false between property probes. A
present "warn" limit followed by an absent "error" limit therefore left the
stale `found` set and incorrectly asserted set[i]. Assign it from the read
result directly.
---
diff --git a/drivers/regulator/fwnode_regulator.c b/drivers/regulator/fwnode_regulator.c
index da809a0..d3ae3b1 100644
--- a/drivers/regulator/fwnode_regulator.c
+++ b/drivers/regulator/fwnode_regulator.c
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@ static void fwnode_get_regulator_prot_limits(struct fwnode_handle *np,
 				struct regulation_constraints *constraints)
 {
 	u32 pval;
-	int i, ret;
+	int i;
 	static const char *const props[] = {
 		"regulator-oc-%s-microamp",
 		"regulator-ov-%s-microvolt",
@@ -64,11 +64,9 @@ static void fwnode_get_regulator_prot_limits(struct fwnode_handle *np,
 
 		for (j = 0; j < ARRAY_SIZE(lvl); j++) {
 			snprintf(prop, 255, props[i], lvl[j]);
-			ret = fwnode_property_read_u32(np, prop, &pval);
-			if (!ret) {
+			found = !fwnode_property_read_u32(np, prop, &pval);
+			if (found)
 				fill_limit(l[j], pval);
-				found = true;
-			}
 			set[i] |= found;
 		}
 	}
